WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.309
The screenwriter of 2011's Green Lantern has
finally gotten around to seeing Deadpool 2

00:00:05.309 --> 00:00:08.940
- and when he stuck around for the credits,
he got an unexpected surprise.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.790
One of the highlights of Deadpool 2 is the
collection of epilogue scenes cut into its

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.020
credit sequence, in which Reynolds' Wade Wilson
travels back through time to fix the mistakes

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.020
of the past.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.940
And the mistakes aren't just from the movie
- they're also mistakes from the real Ryan

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:22.940
Reynolds' career.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.070
One of the jokey scenes sees Wilson go back
in time to the moment when Ryan Reynolds first

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:32.119
reads the script for the critically reviled
2011 superhero film Green Lantern, which wound

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:34.140
up bombing at the box office.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.910
So in order to make sure this reality never
actually comes to pass, Deadpool shoots the

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.940
real-life Reynolds in the head, spraying blood
all over the pages of the Green Lantern script.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.220
"If you could rate the Green Lantern on a
scale of 1 to 10?"

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.060
"One!

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:47.780
It's a one!"

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.780
"It's a one!"

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.680
The scene has left audiences roaring with
laughter - but imagine how it'd feel to be

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.820
Marc Guggenheim, one of the screenwriters
for the Green Lantern movie, watching the

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:57.829
scene play out.

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:01.270
Actually, you don't have to imagine, because
Guggenheim shared his response on Twitter

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.560
after finally seeing Deadpool 2, saying

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.989
"Just saw Deadpool 2.

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:07.180
Well played, @VancityReynolds.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.320
Well played."

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.920
It's a professional response to a pretty savage
joke, but you shouldn't feel too bad for Guggenheim.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.640
Not only does he share the credit - and the
blame - for the Green Lantern script with

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:21.200
three other writers, he's also gone on to
great success since then as one of the architects

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.770
behind the CW's successful Arrowverse.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.030
So he can take a joke.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.100
Meanwhile, Warner Bros. is planning to reboot
the Green Lantern franchise, promising to

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.670
do it right this time.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:31.670
But if they don't?

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:32.810
Well, no problem.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:35.350
After all, Deadpool still has that time machine.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.350
Thanks for watching!

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.729
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:40.950
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

